__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
# The graph store. `.nexus/` also holds config.toml and ontology.toml,
# which are the project's own settings and DO belong in the repo — so the
# derived artefacts are ignored by name, not the directory. (Ignoring the
# directory would also stop git descending into it, hiding the settings.)
.nexus/graph.db
.nexus/graph.json
.nexus/traces/
*.db
# Everything under .claude/ is machine-local EXCEPT rules/, which are
# instruction-authority and belong to the repo — a rule that vanishes on
# clone cannot guide the next contributor, agent or human. Git will not
# descend into an ignored directory, so the contents are ignored rather
# than the directory itself.
.claude/*
!.claude/rules/
# NOTE: the tracked `.claude/rules/nexus-tools.md` is a SYMLINK into
# sphinxcontrib/nexus/rules/ — we dogfood the shipped copy rather than
# keeping a second one. See CLAUDE.md. Do not replace it with a file.
# Sphinx output for nexus's own docs (includes the self-graph).
docs/_build/
